---
// Terms of Service — PLACEHOLDER.
//
// This page exists so the consent checkbox in the enrollment flow links to a
// real URL instead of a 404. The enrollment flow asks people to agree to these
// terms, so the page they're agreeing to must at minimum resolve and say
// honestly that it isn't finished yet.
//
// Real content is a separate follow-up — source material and the open
// questions for the attorney are in docs/legal-source.md.
//
// Per docs/AUNT-MABEL.md § Entity & naming: the contracting party is
// TrustLight, the for-profit operator. Cajun Navy Ground Force appears only as
// the named disaster-response PARTNER — never as the operator or the party you
// contract with. An earlier version of this page named Cajun Relief Foundation
// as the operator; that was wrong and is corrected here.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalDraft from '../components/LegalDraft.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of Service · Aunt Mabel" noindex={true}>
  <LegalDraft heading="Terms of Service" kicker="Legal">
    <p>
      These Terms will govern your use of the Aunt Mabel daily wellness-call
      service, which is operated by <strong>TrustLight</strong>. TrustLight is
      the company you contract with and the company that takes payment.
    </p>
    <p>
      The in-person wellness check after a disaster is carried out by
      <strong>Cajun Navy Ground Force</strong>, our disaster-response partner.
      Aunt Mabel uses their name with their permission. They are a partner in
      this service, not its operator.
    </p>
    <p>
      They're being finalized with counsel now. When they're ready, this page
      will carry the full Terms in plain language, covering what the service
      does and doesn't promise, how billing and cancellation work, and what
      happens to a call schedule during a disaster.
    </p>
    <p>
      Until then, one thing is worth saying plainly, because it's the point
      people most need to understand before they sign up:
    </p>
    <p class="emphasis">
      Aunt Mabel is a friendly daily check-in. It is not an emergency service,
      a medical service, or a monitoring service, and it is not a substitute
      for calling 911 or for professional care.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you have a question in the meantime, please get in touch before
      enrolling rather than after.
    </p>
  </LegalDraft>
</BaseLayout>
